Rem ==================================================================
Rem dict.shoddy — Shoddy standard library: dictionaries
Rem
Rem a dictionary is a List Of Pair (key in Fst, value in Snd) — an
Rem association list. Keys are compared with = so they can be numbers,
Rem strings, booleans, or records. Pure: DictPut and DictDel return new
Rem dictionaries. Fine for hundreds of entries; a hashed implementation
Rem could replace this behind the same words if scale ever demands it.
Rem
Rem     Let d = DictPut(DictPut({ }, "ADA", 96), "LIN", 78)
Rem     DictGet(d, "ADA")            ' 96
Rem ==================================================================

Include "seq.shoddy"

Def DictHas(d As List Of Pair, k As t) As Boolean
    Any(d, Fn(p) => Fst(p) = k)

Def DictGet(d As List Of Pair, k As t) As u
    If IsEmpty(d) Then
        Error("DICTGET: KEY NOT FOUND")
    Else
        If Fst(First(d)) = k Then
            Snd(First(d))
        Else
            DictGet(Rest(d), k)

Def DictGetOr(d As List Of Pair, k As t, dflt As u) As u
    If DictHas(d, k) Then
        DictGet(d, k)
    Else
        dflt

Def DictDel(d As List Of Pair, k As t) As List Of Pair
    Filter(d, Fn(p) => Fst(p) <> k)

Def DictPut(d As List Of Pair, k As t, v As u) As List Of Pair
    Prepend(Pair(k, v), DictDel(d, k))

Def DictKeys(d As List Of Pair) As List Of t
    Map(d, Fst)

Def DictVals(d As List Of Pair) As List Of u
    Map(d, Snd)
